  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burundi Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Burundi Country Programme works to strengthen Burundi&apos;s trade competitiveness and deepen its integration into regional and global markets, building on over a decade of engagement since 2011. The Programme supports modernisation of trade systems and institutions, including continued collaboration with the Burundi Revenue Authority (OBR) on customs digitisation and the Electronic Single Window, while advancing the competitiveness of key export value chains such as coffee, tea, and horticulture. Interventions also target the trade and investment environment through AfCFTA alignment, standards accreditation via the Bureau Burundais de Normalisation et Contr&#xf4;le de la Qualit&#xe9; (BBN), and expanded market access for SMEs, with a deliberate focus on inclusive participation including women traders and cross-border trade actors.</narrative>
  </description>
